Celestial — upstream source and local adaptations

Upstream: https://github.com/geraldo-netto/celestial
Pinned revision: 0e2bb383bc7b1b20112bd9ef6b01e7548bf09eb2
Original author, as declared by the upstream Cargo workspace: geraldo-netto

The original Cargo workspace and core manifests declare AGPL-3.0-or-later.
The original README describes the project as AGPL-3.0. The pinned upstream
tree does not contain a separate LICENSE file. The LICENSE included here
contains the unmodified GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 text.
This distribution preserves the original licensing; it does not relicense
the upstream work or claim ownership of its authors' contributions.

The core source and its public APIs originate in that upstream revision.
Local changes add a complete wasm-bindgen interface, standalone build and
test tooling, WASM-compatible test execution, and a TypeScript vector chart
library. UPSTREAM-README.md preserves the original project description.
Existing source notices and original author metadata remain in place.

Corresponding source for this distribution is included alongside the built
JavaScript, WebAssembly and TypeScript declarations: core/, wasm/, charts/,
tests/, scripts/, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and rust-toolchain.toml. Development
tools are pinned in package.json and the source checkout's package-lock.json.
The npm archive carries the identical lock as npm-shrinkwrap.json, npm's
supported lockfile format for distributions.
The runtime package has no JavaScript dependencies. Third-party development
tools and Rust crates retain their respective licenses and are identified
in the npm and Cargo lockfiles.
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt reproduces the original license and copyright texts
for the locked registry crates in the WASM release dependency graph, with
their declared licenses, versions and source repositories. Regenerate it
with npm run licenses after updating those dependencies.
